NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1025,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,4,3,2,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.5192,"rank":0.0805,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ022008","role":"top","render":{"description":"An old spinster often had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. Once she refused to give way to","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20911","half":"top"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ045418","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It is a forewarning. Ticking can often be heard too. That is also a forewarning: a house will later be renovated.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ111402","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"But when they go to look, the neighbour is simply asleep. The mother suspects that something is going to happen. It was indeed an omen: ten weeks later the neighbour's child drowns and the same wailing is heard.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ123209","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Nurses are often keen to get cauls because carrying one keeps them safe. (After all, if you carry a caul, you are bulletproof.) Cauls are also often sold on. Many Freemasons are said to have a caul.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0489"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CBAK0432","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The next day the neighbour's house on the side that was hot is on fire.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0491"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ022008","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"something she saw coming, and she got a crack in her head. When she grew too old to get out of bed at night, she opened the curtains and saw everything through the window.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ019214","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"These are omens: shortly afterwards her little sister is killed in a traffic accident. The funeral takes place exactly as the girl saw it earlier.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"CJ065302","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He stepped over it. Two weeks later an old fellow from the neighbourhood died, and the hearse really came by.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"CJ007616","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The man pulls him aside when a funeral procession passes. The narrator does not see the procession.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"CJ109402","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The door and the gate are opened, and he is driven to a house where someone has died. On the way back the gate is opened for him again, but he has seen no one.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"CJ111119","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"They were the portents of the later bicycle, car and train lights. Other people saw the train running before the railway was there. It was a vision of the future.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"CJ014011","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The next day the train from Leeuwarden to Groningen ran for the first time.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0492"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"DYKFRIES2201","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Likewise, here and there people heard the roar of trains, years before there was any talk of railways in Friesland.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0492"},"home":"1-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The top piece breaks off in mid-sentence. The bottom one finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0481. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c6"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c6"],"stack":["c1","c6"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3058,"rank":0.6075,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ046312","role":"member","render":{"description":"Never run in the middle of the road at night: a funeral procession may pass.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24424","original":"Wy woarden altyd warskôge: rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje passeare.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ102104","role":"member","render":{"description":"Some people had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. You should never run in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37102","original":"Yn 'e Harkema en yn Stiensgea ha 'k wol guon kend dy't nachts fan bêd moesten om lykstaesjes to sjen.\nMen moest nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2266","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"You were warned not to walk in the cart track or on the bridle path at night. Because there you could meet evil spirits.","place":"Heesselt","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/127631","original":"Dat weet ik ook nog. Je werd gewaarschuwd om 's nachts niet in 't wagenspoor of in 't paardenpad te lopen. Want daar kon je de boze geesten tegenkomen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ052415","role":"member","render":{"description":"The narrator tells of two men who often saw funeral processions. You must never walk in the middle of the road, because an invisible funeral procession can drive you off the road.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25234","original":"Douwe Stavasius fan Grinzer Pein seach lykstaesjes.\nBoardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane ek. Dy leeft noch.\nMen mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme, sûnder dat men it sjocht. Dan wurde jo fan 'e wei ôfsmiten.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Heesselt belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.0963,"rank":0.0502,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ100119","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Some children are born with a caul. They later saw everything. They could foresee death, like my uncle, who had already seen the deaths of all seven of his children in the form of little coffins on the floor.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"TM 2901","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36754","original":"Der binne bern dy wurde mei de helm geboaren. As se dy helm nei boven ta fan 't gesicht lûke, sjogge se letter alles.\nIk haw in skoansuster to Westergeast to wenjen. Dêr njonken wennet in frou dy is mei de helm geboaren.\nIn omke fan my sjocht de dea ek foarút. 't Is in Wybenga.\nSawn kear hat er in bern forlern en alle sawn kearen hat er fan tofoaren de kiste oer de flier stean sjoen. 't Is in broer fan mem. Hy wennet yn 'e Westerein.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ111712","role":"omen","render":{"description":"The seventh of seven sons is born with a caul.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29923","original":"Bontsje Keke wie mei de helm geboaren. De sawnde soan fan sawn soannen wie mei de helm geboaren.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ036709","role":"omen","render":{"description":"One of seven boys always has to get up at night to see things. He is clairvoyant.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22922","original":"Jasper en Jinke fan 'e Boelensloane hienen sawn jonges. Ien fan dy sawn jonges moest nachts ta 't hûs út om hwat to sjen. Dat wie Gerke Veenstra.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","7 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":7},"on_success":{"chime":7,"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.6258,"rank":0.0,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL000404","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Seeing a witte juffer (white lady); playing at being a witte juffer with a white sheet around oneself.","place":"Ingen","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209537","original":"Witte vrouwen . Bij de pas (aanplant van wilgen of populieren met onderhout van elzen en essen) (lag dicht bij de woning van de zegslieden) zag men soms een witte gedaante lopen. Maar sommigen geloofden niet aan de witte juffer, zo werd Han Briene er van verdacht, dat hij soms de kinderen bang wilde maken door voor witte juffer te spelen (hij deed zich dan een laken om) Enige jongens wilden met Jas Gaosbeek, een niet volwaardige zoon van een bakker, een grap uithalen. Zij sloegen zich lakens om en gingen wandelen op een plaats, waar Jas passeren moest. Deze ging er echter niet voor door, maar begon de \"juffer\", die hij het eerst te pakken kreeg af te ranselen. De andere jongens sloegen toen op de vlucht","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL002208","role":"variant","render":{"description":"In the evening, mistaking a stick with a newspaper on it for a witte juffer (white lady).","place":"Ochten","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210065","original":"Er moet een witte juffer gelopen hebben op het Zand (fruitteeltbedrijf) bij het witte hek (dit stond op de weg, die tussen twee kolken doorloopt. Keuken, hij was toen 18 jaar, ging eens met een kameraad naar Eldik (buurtschap) om een vriend te bezoeken. Deze bleek niet thuis. Op de dijk op de plaats waar beneden het witte hek stond, was een stok met krant er om gezet, als teken voor de castreur dat er \"keujes\" moesten gesneden worden. Janus stapte tegen deze stok aan, deze ging heen en weer, de kameraad beweerde, dat hij een witte juffer had gezien en was van dit idee, ook de volgende dag, niet af te brengen","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"HOL002604","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A white maiden who asks the way throws a hat full of money and disappears.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210163","original":"Berend, den dakuil (een Van Uden) smeerde de daken van binnen aan met kalk, vandaar dat hij deze bijnaam kreeg. Eens liep Berend op de Grotebrugse grintweg bij de Twaalf Apostelen (straatje) toen een witte juffer hem de weg vroeg naar het veer. Berend zei haar die en nadat hij dit gedaan had, gooide zij hem de hoed vol met \"Berliner daolder\". Driemaal was Berend dit overkomen. Bij het veer gekomen wilde Berend haar bedanken, maar hij kreeg geen kans daartoe: zij was verdwenen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Gelderland an object was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1962.","That card names an object. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"42352bd4b1ef7dc6","accepted_hashes":["0f2efd4ea01cce01f03a869f94b1238866f226d4ccd7e5e9a69d04f93dd86bbb","2ef74508f35e5713f590573cd629455b3b73597b7adb47823769f93450af6529","6689d7d5f826ef1f3595ae58f129f7014552af28ee4aeb097df1462403622e89","a1e9b581f5768d050047c1254e1ea273ef47d328b1b6e1d0c7f0057bcebee813","d07ed9473c1655acf66191e89cc2ac6d4896bef688dbd1bd2fe2b976c0f9fea2","db8c5f72e4fe90b99e9a5ca655cab94b865fe3e62d8d634b18b9e12729476df2"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3535,"rank":1.0009,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KEUNING011705","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A white apparition stands still in the middle of a little bridge.","place":"Easternijtsjerk","prov":"Fr.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131602","original":"Sa seach ien hjir ek ris sa 'n forskining midden op in planke, dy oer de sleat laei, stean. Mar dy bleau dêr stiif stean, dat de man is werom gien.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ020208","role":"member","render":{"description":"One evening people once saw two witte wijven (white women).","place":"Jistrum","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20586","original":"Freark en Wytske wennen op 'e Iest to Jistrum. Ik wenne yn dy tiid by de boer, 'k wie fyftsjin jier. Hja fortelden op in joun, se hienen to jounpraten west. Doe't se weromkommen en op 'e hoeke wienen, hienen dêr twa âlde wite wiven west.\nSy hienen deabinaud west en koenen foar noch achterút. In hiel skoft bleauwen se stean. Doe't se letter thús kommen wienen se noch sa forbouwerearre, dat sy koenen earst net in wurd útbringe.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ035001","role":"member","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot a white lady on a horse used to be seen often. She is a ghost woman.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22709","original":"Op 'e Lytse Wei by de Harkema ried froeger in wite dame op in hynder, doe wie de Lytse Wei noch in sânpaed.\nDurk Pitstra hat har us njonken him hawn op in joun, doe siet er op syn eigen hynder om dat yn 't lân to bringen. Hwat hurder hy ried, hwat hurder dat frommes tasette. Hy koe har net kwyt wurde en dreau op 't lêst yn 't swit.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ045113","role":"member","render":{"description":"Witte wieven (white women) used to haunt a haunted spot.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24238","original":"Op dit ein fan 'e Folgerster loane spoeken froeger wite wiven.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Easternijtsjerk belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.1221,"rank":0.9322,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST041","role":"card","render":{"description":"Some farmers see a white figure standing against a tree in the evening. They are badly frightened because they think it is the ill-omened figure of a wit wief (white lady). Later they see that the figure is not a wit wief but a white goat standing with its legs against the tree, eating the leaves.","place":"Mijdrecht","prov":"Utr.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13255","original":"Witte Juffers, Varende Vrouwen\nHet enigste wat ik mij daarover herinner is, dat ik mij het verhaal herinner, hoe enige boeren, thuis terugkerende van een burenavondje, geschrokken waren van een witte figuur bij een hek en boom, wat een op haar achterpoten staande geit bleek te zijn, die aan de boomtakken knabbelde. Het blè geluid had hun echter gerustgesteld en nog bevende waren zij door het hek gegaan en de geit gepasseerd. Zij dachten dat het een der witte wieven was, iets wat een onheilbrengende ervaring zou zijn. Ik was toen ongeveer 10 á 12 jaren oud. Mijn ouders wisten mij geen antwoord te geven, maar mijn grootmoeder zei dat men er niet over mocht praten en het zien van witte wieven ongeluk zou brengen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ103913","role":"card","render":{"description":"One evening a man thought he recognised his niece in a woman coming towards him. However, he was lifted up and thrown away, after which the woman floated off.","place":"Drogeham","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37327","original":"It gebeurde op 'e Ikkers op in joun dat Harm Hamstra bûtendoar kaem en in frommeske seach. Hy miende dat it syn nichtsje wie, in jongfaem fan sa'n tweintich jier: Wytske Hamstra, dy't letter troude mei Elle Wijma fan Eastemar. Hja kaem him yn 'e mjitte.\nHy sei: \"Bistû dêr noch, Wytske?\"\nMar dyselde sei neat werom. Ynpleats dêrfan wied er opnom woarn en in ein fuortsmiten en dat frommeske wie swevend fuortrekke.\nOp 'e weromreis kom er wer by ús tolânne. 't Ljocht wie by ús noch op. Doe hat ús heit him dat út brocht hwant hy doarst dêr net wer allinne lâns.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"sill","render":{"description":"A farmer has two sons. One cannot be got out of bed in the morning, the other has to do all the work. At some point he is fed up with it and wants to wake his brother up properly. In doing so he hits him on the temple, and his brother dies. The family moves away because they can no longer cope. The linden tree has kept on blooming. The murdered boy still haunts the area.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0311","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12173","stain":"two"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ZEEUW054","role":"card","render":{"description":"At fort Ronduute a woman appears every 100 years. She asked a passer-by to come with her to the cellar of the fort. There were 3 chests, with a dog on one and on the 2nd a lion holding the key to the 3rd in its mouth, which the man has to take. He does not dare, and the woman takes leave for 100 years.","place":"Overslag","prov":"Zl.","year":1923,"code":"SINSAG 0301","initials":"D.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38980","original":"Witte Juffers\n\nOnder de gemeente Overslag stond 'n kasteel, dat men de \"Ronduute\" noemde.\nHier verschijnt om de honderd jaar, 's nachts om twaalf uur, een vrouw. Eens kwam er juist een man voorbij, aan wien ze vroeg of hij mee wilde gaan naar de kelder van het fort Ronduute. Daar bevonden zich drie koffers. Op den eenen koffer zat een hond, op den anderen een leeuw met den sleutel van den derden koffer in zijn muil. Als hij nu dien sleutel uit den muil van den leeuw kon trekken, zou hij al het goud krijgen, dat in dien derden koffer zat. Hij durfde het echter niet aan. Toen zei de vrouw: \"Adieu, tot over honderd jaar\" en verdween weer.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ109330","role":"card","render":{"description":"Hauntings by a witte juffer (white lady) and a white lady","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38446","original":"Yn Feanwâlden spokke in wite juffer, seinen se en op 'e Godleas Singel spokke in wite dame.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"BIJLSMA007506","role":"card","render":{"description":"Sighting of a woman dressed in white with a veil, travelling in a spinning butter tub.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310F","initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130656","original":"Alde Houwing fan Sumar wie in \"wedergeboren man\". Houwing wie op in moaije simmermoarn oan de marswâl to melken mei in faem en in jonge. Hja seagen op it wetter hwat oankommen. It wie to lyts foar in boatsje, it like wol in bûteraed. Dêr siet it boppe-ein fan in frommiske yn, by de mul omt-ôf alhiel yn it wyt, mei in wale oer de holle. It boatsje bigoun as in top to draeijen. Houwing en de beide oaren wienen op it lân delfallen. Doe 't hja wer seagen, wie it skynsel fuort. It barde by Sumar mids de 19 de ieu.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Goutum. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c3","object":"window","text":"Goutum"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c3","word":"two","stained":"c3"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P1","difficulty":1.1309,"rank":0.9121,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"EDJSL003","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand tells his girl that he has an errand to run, and that if she meets a vicious dog she must give it her handkerchief. She does indeed meet a dog, throws the handkerchief at it and flees. During the meal it is seen that he has pieces of a handkerchief between his teeth. When his room is searched, the belt that turns someone into a werewolf is found. As soon as the belt is thrown into the fire, the farmhand, who was working far away, is standing by the oven trying to jump into the fire. After the belt has burned, the farmhand is released.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1894,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"E.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9505","original":"De weerwolf\nEr was eens een boerenknecht die soms een weerwolf was.\nDe knecht vrijde met een van de meiden, maar zij wist van de prins geen kwaad. Op een keer waren ze een eind buiten het dorp gaan wandelen. Toen ze op huis aangingen, viel de schemer in.\nOpeens had de knecht zin weerwolf te worden.\nHij zei tegen de meid: \"Ik moet hier even een boodschap doen. Loop jij maar vast door, ik haal je wel in. Mocht je een kwade hond tegenkomen, die je wil bijten, gooi hem dan mijn zakdoek toe. Dan heeft hij iets om zijn tanden in te zetten, terwijl jij ervandoor gaat.\"\nHij ging weg, en een poosje later zag ze een grote hond op zich afkomen. Ze gooide hem de zakdoek toe en zette het op een lopen. Het dier scheurde de zakdoek aan flarden en at hem op. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BOEKV179","role":"card","render":{"description":"A youth is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the youth's teeth. Werewolves always wear a band around their waist. The farmer the youth works for burns the band. The werewolf still tries to get into the fire, but he is held back. When the band has burned, the youth is an ordinary person again.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1896,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"G.J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35060","original":"Van een Weerwolf.\n\nOp de Achterste hoef woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op een eigenaardige manier zijn ze daar achter gekomen.\nDie knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buiten dorps (1) geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet meer zoo heel ver van huis toen voelde hij een onweerstaanbare lust om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte het natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens (2) van den weg af bij genen boer zijn; ga gij maar door: ik zal u wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die op u aan bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij misschien wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"SINBRABSAG185","role":"card","render":{"description":"A young man is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the young man's teeth. This is how they know he is a werewolf.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46940","original":"No. 185. Op de Achterste hoef bij Bladel woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op 'n vreemde manier zijn ze dat aan de weet gekomen. Die knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buitendorps geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker, toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet ver meer van huis toen hij een onweerstaanbaren lust voelde om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte dat natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens van den weg af bij genen boer zijn, ga gij maar door: ik zal oe wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die naar oe bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST009","role":"card","render":{"description":"A couple go for a walk in the evening. The boy has to relieve himself, but before he disappears into the bushes he advises the girl that if a beast attacks her, she should throw her handkerchief in front of its mouth. A dangerous beast does indeed come at the girl. She throws her handkerchief in front of its jaws and the beast tears it apart. When the boy comes back, the girl sees that he has remnants of her handkerchief between his teeth. She now knows he is a werewolf and tells him so. The boy disappears and never came back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13223","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen vrijer bracht 's avonds z'n meisje naar huis. Onderweg zei ie: \"Ik moet even mijn behoefte doen. Als je in tussentijd een dier of zoiets op je af ziet komen, gooi het dan je zakdoek voor z'n kop.\" Toen de jongen weg was, kwam er een dier op het meisje aangelopen. Ze slingerde haar zakdoek voor z'n muil en het beest verscheurde hem. Even later kwam de jongen terug en hij vroeg zijn meisje of er iets gebeurd was. Ze vertelde wat er was voorgevalllen en terwijl keek ze hem strak aan. Toen zei ze hem: \"Ik geloof, dat jij het beest bent geweest, want je hebt de stukken zakdoek nog tussen je tanden zitten\" Onmiddellijk was de vrijer verdwenen, en het meisje heeft hem nooit teruggezien.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is an object.","Begins with H. 12 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"42352bd4b1ef7dc6","accepted_hashes":["71aecc88a09207ca3efcf39667697c9ca15784ea031934bbc202b11f47d5077c","95a31c4977340e636714c14a7269d17ce8859a79b79023977fda37a70fe8b9bc","c7b161e3f979b9035f6d67a1e74f2b22d5584cdf92ebaea60b9517f98cf110c4","dc15b487add1d1508d9c61612b6513afe1a234fef7bf7e2ed3f8c6847708ce47"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1893,"rank":0.6707,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ030809","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A group of boys relieving themselves in a field are startled by a white lady. It is a ghost. They run off with their trousers undone.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21975","original":"Wy wienen fan dy jonge baeskes. Wy moesten allegear tagelyk út 'e broek. Wy gongen 't lân yn. Wy hienen krekt de broek los of dêr kom in wite dame oan. Dy kom op ús yn. 't Wie in spoek. Wy binne allegear nei de wei ta roan mei de broeken los.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ109209","role":"member","render":{"description":"Of seven boys in a family, one is a werewolf. Of seven girls in a family, one is a nightmare.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38395","original":"Fan sawn jonges út ien gesin is ien in wjerwolf.\nFan sawn famkes út ien gesin is ien in nachtmerje.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ111512","role":"member","render":{"description":"A nightmare is a little woman who can enter the house through every little hole. Of seven girls in one household, one is a nightmare. Of seven boys, one is a werewolf.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29774","original":"In nachtmerje is in frommeske, dat troch alle gatsjes yn 'e hûs komme kin.\nFan 'e sawn famkes út ien húsgesin is ien in nachtmerje.\nFan 'e sawn jonges út ien húsgesin is ien in wjerwolf.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ109517","role":"member","render":{"description":"Of seven boys in a family, one is a werewolf. A werewolf is always out and about. A werewolf and a nightmare do the same things; a nightmare is a woman. Someone troubled by a nightmare should sprinkle himself with flour.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38494","original":"Fan sawn jonges út ien húshâlding is ien in wjerwolf.\nWjerwolven matte der altyd op út. Dy ha in ploech.\nIn nachtmerje en in wjerwolf is it selde. In wjerwolf is in man, in nachtmerje is in frommeske. Mar se dogge beide itselde.\nMen kin se fange. As je lêst fan in nachtmerje ha mat men jin mei moal bistruije.\nHjir yn 'e Westerein wenne in man dy hie gauris lêst fan in nachtmerje. Doe bistruide er him mei moal. Doe kom de nachtmerje en dy krige moal oan har. Doe koe se net wer fuortkomme, hwant in nachtmerje mei neat meinimme. Doe't de man de oare moarns wekker waerd, siet de nachtmerje op 'e hoeke fan it bêd.\nIt wie in bikende frou út 'e Westerein. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Augustinusga belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.064,"rank":0.5641,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"ENGELS001721","role":"card","render":{"description":"Man has to walk around with a werewolf for two days.","place":"Grashoek","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210547","original":"Weerwolven:\nIk heb eens horen vertellen van een man in Kessel, die twee dagen met een weerwolf op zijn rug moest lopen. Hij werd hem eindelijk kwijt, door hem tussen twee dicht bijeen staande bomen af te wringen. Hij had de klauwsporen op zijn borst staan.\n\nVerslag 50, Omzetting van de verhalen, verteld door Leonardus Kluijtmans, Helden, doorgegeven onder no. L291-17, op 26-12-1962. Van Nederl. versie in plaatselijk dialect. Helden, 4 nov. 1969\nIch heb èns huuëre vertèlle van enne mins in Kèèssel, dè twieë daag mèt te wèèrwolf hei motten drage. Hè woord öm kwiet, dor öm tössen twieë buim, die kort bei-ein sjtonge, van de rök te vringe. Later hei ’n de klauwsjpóre nag op zien boorst staon.","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"door","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ097534","role":"card","render":{"description":"One in seven brothers is a werewolf. One lived near Drachten who had to murder someone every so often.","place":"Sumar","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36271","original":"Fan sawn bruorren is ien in wjerwolf. Op 'e ein fan 'e Drachtster Dwarsfeart hat ien wenne. Dy moest bytiden ien formoardzje.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LYST008","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every night at exactly twelve o'clock a farmhand takes a small hoop out of the lime tree. He hangs the hoop around his neck and turns into a werewolf. He roams about for a while and tears apart everything that comes near him. After that he becomes an ordinary person again. The farmer finds his behaviour strange and asks the priest for advice. The priest realises that the farmhand is a werewolf and advises the farmer to send the farmhand on an errand from which he can never be back home by midnight. On the agreed night the priest takes the hoop out of the tree at midnight. The farmhand is standing under that tree and sees everything. He flees and never comes back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0803","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13222","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen boerenknecht kroop 's nachts klokslag 12 uur in de lindenboom voor de boerderij. Boven in de boom hing voor gewone mensen onzichtbaar een hoepeltje. Dat hing de knecht om zijn hals. Als ie uit de boom geklauterd was, liep ie in de gedaante van een hond weg en verscheurde alles wat hem in de weg kwam. Als ie een tijd zo rondgelopen had, was ie weer gewoon mens. Na een tijd was het de boer, bij wie de weerwolf in dienst was, opgevallen, dat zijn knecht nacht op nacht weg was. Hij ging naar de pastoor en die had het zaakje meteen door. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","3 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c3","object":"door","n":3},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":4,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.2994,"rank":0.415,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KUSTERS008908","role":"target","render":{"description":"A dead person must haunt until a wrong done during life has been made right.","place":null,"prov":"N.-Br.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"C.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/207357","original":"'n Boerenmeid zag op de stal 'n geest terwijl ze melkte. 't Bleek de overleden vrouw des huizes. Tijdens haar leven had ze gestolen; ze moest komen spoken tot dat onrecht was goed gemaakt.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BLECOURTNB0007","role":"helper","render":{"description":"The punishment of a man who falsely swears that he is indicating the boundary between two places is that after his death he must wander with a glowing head at the place where he dared to swear the oath.","place":"Veldhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1883,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"J.C.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50001","original":"1.7. De gloeiende man\nVoor 'n veertig jaren nog kon men iederen avond of nacht een spook zien, dat steeds heen en weer liep in de Strijpsche hei van de boerderij 'den Tegenbosch' naar \"t Klotven'. 't Leek een volwassen man met een gloeiend hoofd; vandaar, dat dit spook in deze streken algemeen bekend is onder den naam van 'de gloeiige'. Verschillende personen hebben 't gezien met h'r eigen oogen, o.a. de bewoners van den Tegenbosch en houtrapers, die\n's avonds huiswaarts keerden uit de mastbosschen van Acht. Dat het spook nu niet meer daar ronddwaalt komt, omdat die woeste hei nu ook al is bedekt met mastboseh. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Brabant dialect","front":"description"},"home":"4-1","geo":[51.41833,5.40278]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KUSTERS003715","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Return of a dead person at midnight at a crossroads when he passes a crossroads.","place":"Deurne","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"C.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/47312","original":"Als 'n dode 'n kruisweg gepasseerd was, kwam hij daar terug 's nachts om 12 uur.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"4-1","geo":[51.46,5.79722]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KUSTERS011801","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Around midnight a female figure is seen, a dead sister who has returned.","place":"Asten","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"C.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/207634","original":"De opname is in Tilburgs dialect\n\nVan giste dor heurde tiggeworreg niks mir van. Neen, des iets aanders as spooke en hekse. 't Is weezelek gebeurt. Ik waar nog mer kort in Arnhem en sliep dor op n aauw zaaltje dè mèr heel wènig gebrökt werd. We sliepe dòr toe nog in celle mi gurdène d'r veur; dè wèt te wel net as vruger bij de kweekelinge in Tilbörg. Ik was ne slèchte slòper; ik lag veul wakker. Niemend zee der ièts van, mer as ik 's ovus te bet laag dan bewoog zó heél zuutjes de gurdèn vur de cèl en ging soms 'n bitje oope. Ik zaag ut mer zee niks. Dè gebeurde dikkuls en ik hep d'r nooit iets van gezee mer ne keer heurde ik ze stillekes d’roover pròte. …","lang":"Brabant dialect; Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"4-1","geo":[51.40417,5.74861]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 3 hours’ walk of Veldhoven.","Find Geldrop on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[51.42167,5.55972],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Geldrop"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0354,"rank":0.4433,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL001711","role":"member","render":{"description":"Return of a former occupant after her death.","place":"Kesteren","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209915","original":"Op de Appelenburg (het laatste huis in Ochten naar de kant van Dodewaard, vroeger een kasteel geweest) had eens een vroegere bewoonster gelopen, die al lang overleden was. Tante Vermeer had met haar gepraat, maar deze mocht niet vertellen, wat zij gezegd had. \nEr waren ook 2 mensen langs gekomen met hoge hoeden op. Deze hadden niets gezegd.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL000706","role":"member","render":{"description":"Fear of a baron who walks through the village after his death.","place":"Ommeren","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209633","original":"Baron van Brakel ziet men nog lopen in de Pooijenstraat, vlak bij zijn buiten Den Eng. Hij heeft een lange pijp in zijn mond. De mensen worden bang als ze hem zien, aldus Gaartje (dr. J.M.G. van der Poel heeft over deze persoon, die een pionier was op landbouwgebied, een studie geschreven. Gaartjes oom was zijn vertrouwde)","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"ENGELS002109","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A man is often jumped on by the werewolf.","place":"Neer","prov":"L.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210594","original":"Weerwolf:\nIn Neer was vroeger een “sjnieder” ofwel kleermaker, die bij zijn klanten thuis ging werken. Als hij ’s avonds laat naar huis toe ging werd hij dikwijls door een weerwolf besprongen, die hij dan moest dragen, tot hij thuis was. Hij was dit gesol danig moe. Toen hij weer eens naar huis ging, dacht hij: “Daar komt hij weer! Dit keer zal hij me niet te pakken krijgen.” Hij gooide naar hem met zijn schaar. De weerwolf verdween. ’s Anderendaags had hij spijt dat hij zijn schaar kwijt was, en ging ter plaatse kijken. De schaar stak met de punten in een oude “tor” een knot-eik!\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"GENDT157","role":"member","render":{"description":"Neighbours see their dead neighbour in his house. A family that moves into the house has to deal with haunting, which stops after the house is blessed.","place":"Gendt","prov":"Gld.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"M.H.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50183","original":"Opten Dries wonde Groadus Mielder en nèven ’m wonde zien zwoager Jan Huting. Groadus gieng dood en wier begrave. Op ’n keer was Jan Huting on ’t hout hakke vör de kachel en zien zoon ston nèven’m. Opens zèj die: “Voader, kiek ’s nor ’t huus van ome Groadus. Die kiekt dör ’t raam hirrenopper [hier op aan]”. Jan Huting keek en zag ’t ok duidelijk. Gaauw dornoa wier da huus verkoch on Piet Pruin. Die gieng er mè zien huushoue ien wone. Mar da liep nie bes af. ’t Spoktener. ’s Nachs hörde ze ielke keer kloppe en boke, net of ’t huus afgebroke zou worre. De minse kosseneter*** hos nie mer ien uuthoue. De burluj stonne soaves op ’n afstand van vieftig, zestig meter te luustere. Ze ware ok bang. Da kos nie langer zo. En Pruin gieng nor de pestoor. …","lang":"Gendt dialect (Achterhoek)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Neer belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1339,"rank":0.4583,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBAK0151","role":"top","render":{"description":"An empty farmhouse is haunted; at night a light burns and noises are heard. Finally someone dares to go and look, and he","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1900,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/8760","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BLECOURTNB0052","role":"half","render":{"description":"The ghost disappears when a drunk man tells him to put the post back in its former place.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0404"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ011303","role":"half","render":{"description":"Once a man rode past that old house at five to twelve. There he saw a very large dog. And suddenly the dog was gone again. But on one side there was a hedge, and on the other side water. Where had the dog gone? The place was uncanny and the man became frightened.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CBAK0151","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"sees four card players. When he asks whether they are people or spirits, they answer that they have been waiting for him, because money is buried there that keeps them from leaving. It is unknown whether the treasure was found.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"four"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CBAK0513","role":"half","render":{"description":"The answer is that they have waited a long time for someone, that there is money buried of which he may have a third, and the rest must go in equal parts to the poor and a church congregation. Once the request has been carried out, the haunting stops.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"ZEEUW060","role":"half","render":{"description":"After his death he comes back to haunt. At the spot in the horse stable, where no horse can be kept, a later occupant digs up a treasure.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"VODA_032_11","role":"half","render":{"description":"After her death the woman came to haunt her husband. At the same time of day when he had refused to give her water, she came by and asked for water. The neighbours saw only a yellow patch in front of the window, but the man insisted it was his wife's face.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0434"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The machine stops in mid-sentence. The rest finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c4","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c4"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":4,"card":"c1","word":"four","stained":"c4"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
